{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker","id":1022153,"title":"Scariest Fucker","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-25T17:46:41-08:00","id":1022153,"title":"Scariest Fucker","content":"I'm just wondering which splat or monster is the scariest, not the most powerful, but the scariest? <br /> <br /> I talking about the fucker you'd least like to be in room or alley alone with. <br /> <br /> Is it Vampires, blood drinkers that they are, is it a werewolf who can go into a killing rage when pissed off enough, is the unclean, unnatural Prommies, is it Sin Eaters with their disturbing tag a long voyager they take everywhere with them, is it Mummy, a being so old, they make the pyrimids look young, a mage whose innate curiousity could lead them becoming your personal super powered stalker, Beast well I don't have to explain Beasts do I, demons with their soul pacts, or maybe Changelings or other Far with their alien perpective?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T17:55:25-08:00","id":1022157,"title":"","content":"On a subjective scale, vampires are the only Chronicles monster I can recall having nightmares about. They're always standing over me, talking about how they're going to kill me. And I think also I'm a little scared at the fact that sometimes I think if I were given the offer, I'd let myself be turned.<br /> <br /> Demons themselves aren't all that scary to me, but the God-Machine certainly is. Sometimes I just think about its implications, what it means for it to control the world, how nothing means anything beyond its self-replicating programming, and I feel a frisson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T20:03:19-08:00","id":1022181,"title":"","content":"Slashers. There is nothing scarier than a monster everyone could be, and that truly has no human attachments or even care anymore. (seriously, that book was the only one to really scare the hell out of me).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T21:55:38-08:00","id":1022221,"title":"","content":"Are we talking PC splats only? Cause for me it's probably the Gentry, but in terms of playable templates, I guess it would have to be Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T22:02:47-08:00","id":1022224,"title":"","content":"Probably an idigam.<br /> <br /> I'd find a Promethean unnervingly disgusting to be around. It doesn't seem to be the same kind of scary you were looking for, though, Omegaphallic. A half-formed proto-person whose need to be like you is so great it erodes away the world around it and inflicts maddening obsessions on those it talks to. And of course there's the occasional Torment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T00:17:01-08:00","id":1022241,"title":"","content":"I'll go with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>. As much as other things in the game can scare the hell out of me, Slashers are defined by being anathema to life. Other things are monster on the outside that can become pretty fucked-up, or just be normal people inside. Slashers are monster inside beyond any doubt.<br /> <br /> But there are several ways to be scary. In a certain way, the question isn't fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T01:31:46-08:00","id":1022247,"title":"","content":"Wow, I'd never though I'd go traditionalist here but I've got to say the scaries fuckers to me are the Inferno Demons.<br /> <br /> Honerable mention to Abyssal Entities, because FUCK!, but given the choice between a mind shatteringly horrible anti-reality entity and the personification of humanity's own evil I'd have to say the intimately personal horror wins out over the cosmic horror. Or, to put it more poetically: the Thing that crawled out of the hole in the wall may be The End that seeks ecstacy from the death throws of the world's innocents that's forever denied to it by the infinity of the hole in the wall, but the Whisper that grows in the back of your mind as you try to convince yourself what those monsters needed to die is far more horrifying. Especially after the 7th victim's screams bring to mind the name of the Whisperer, and you no longer know if the demon tricked you to this point or if you were the sole architect of it's throne of gore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 12-26-2016, 04:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T05:55:22-08:00","id":1022288,"title":"","content":"Well, Sybaris makes all Mummies scary by default... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T07:58:29-08:00","id":1022336,"title":"","content":"A pretty low-powered from the rest of what been listed so far. But for me what scared me the most was the cellphone that recharged on fear. I think it was in the mage night horror book. Beyond sentience and doing what any cellphone can do, it didnt have any power to help it. But it had 5 intelligence and that is enough.<br /> Its last owner was found dead of dehydration in a cabin in the woods not 10 meters away from a clean river. He had been convinced by the phone that the river had been poisoned.<br /> <br /> It's no idigam or gentry on power level but it is still a terrifying little part of the chronicles of darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T08:20:28-08:00","id":1022348,"title":"","content":"A fetch, from Changeling. Seriously, I got shivers from typing that just now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T09:38:36-08:00","id":1022376,"title":"","content":"Maybe a more interesting question could be how the things in CoD can be downright scary?<br /> <br /> It would be double interesting to see a short horror story showing the dread of each one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T15:51:48-08:00","id":1022493,"title":"","content":"I would so write those. Would it be cheating to have the horror be partly because it is unclear to the protagonists exactly what kind of monster it is at First? Or if part of the scariness is their cruel personality rather than just their hungers, powers and features?<br /> <br /> Though if we're doing any creature, I'd vote for the Strix. If Humanity 0 vampires with a Lust vice aren't monstrous enough for their desires, I'm terrified of what kind of foul depths of depravity would actually satisfy them. On top of that, no one really knows what they really are. <br /> <br /> And if fansplats are allowed, then any of the various flavors of corrupted Nobles, whether Storms, Tears, Mirrors or just Low Belief are the worst.<br /> <br /> My momma always quoted an author who said to fear the person who is absolutely sure they are in the right more than you fear an admitted monster. And the scariest monster is the one who is something you could become without even knowing it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T16:16:18-08:00","id":1022508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1022493#post1022493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My momma always quoted an author who said to fear the person who is absolutely sure they are in the right more than you fear an admitted monster. And the scariest monster is the one who is something you could become without even knowing it</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, a fanatic and zealous hunter. At least the 'real' monsters come to admit they're the monsters in horror stories, even the more human ones like mages and sin-eaters. And if the hunter turns into a Slasher......<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T17:59:21-08:00","id":1022557,"title":"","content":"I could say that for the purpose of this idea, it is good that the horror comes somehow from the nature of the &quot;monster&quot;, but &quot;somehow&quot; is the key word. In the end, it have just to be interesting to read.<br /> <br /> And after some stories, some &quot;victims/witnesses&quot; can be previously used monsters, for a shift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T02:21:30-08:00","id":1022661,"title":"","content":"Incarnate Beast who is the Apex of the region probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T03:15:14-08:00","id":1022673,"title":"","content":"You can't go wrong with a Screaming Moon Cahalith","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T06:23:58-08:00","id":1022716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1022508#post1022508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that case, a fanatic and zealous hunter. At least the 'real' monsters come to admit they're the monsters in horror stories, even the more human ones like mages and sin-eaters. And if the hunter turns into a Slasher......</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but a Low-Belief and/or Dark Court Noble is that with (lower-cost) superpowers and the emotional inability to not intervene and enforce their will.<br /> <br /> Plus, the Dethroned are almost a metaphor for what people with clinical depression like me are terrified of becoming. Trapped by the tragedies of their past and self-destructive patterns, they drag everyone else down with them until the world is truly as hopeless and grey as they knew it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T11:46:52-08:00","id":1022871,"title":"","content":"Geists scare the hell out of me. Not the sin-eater, they always struck me as cool. But the actual geists? No thanks, that concept is just fucked up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T13:39:49-08:00","id":1022931,"title":"","content":"Beasts are literally humanity's primal fears given form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:58:53-08:00","id":1022974,"title":"","content":"but that doesn't mean they're good at it, or at least, it doesn't mean they can't be outclassed. Someone with a phobia of poisonous snakes is still gonna be more scared of the giant rampaging wolfman eating bullets like candy and ripping apart steel doors, even if there are also snakes in the room","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:58:55-08:00","id":1022975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1022931#post1022931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beasts are literally humanity's primal fears given form.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're people possessed by such beings. Their apparent form is pretty mundane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:00:39-08:00","id":1022978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1022975#post1022975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're people possessed by such beings. Their apparent form is pretty mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it was something more than possession. Like, that was part of their heritage. Having them be possessed by alien beings form the realms of beyond makes them sound too conceptually similar to Sin-Eaters to my ears","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:06:57-08:00","id":1022985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1022978#post1022978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was something more than possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not Possession like the Manifestation of ephemerals, but their soul's been devoured and replaced by the Horror. In some media this is what possession leads to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like, that was part of their heritage. Having them be possessed by alien beings form the realms of beyond makes them sound too conceptually similar to Sin-Eaters to my ears </div> </div> </div>It's unclear whether the person was destined for it or not. But the difference between them and Sin-Eaters is the same, as the geist is a separate being that can, at least in first edition, be cleaved from the host. A Beast's Horror is more entwined with them, if anything it would be closer to werewolf, with a spirit of fear instead of the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-27-2016, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T05:38:07-08:00","id":1023205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1022975#post1022975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They're people possessed by such beings. Their apparent form is pretty mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://stancarey.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/jef-mallett-frazz-comic-strip-detention-for-tomato-semantics.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:11:51-08:00","id":1023221,"title":"","content":"Actually, &quot;possession&quot; describes a fair amount of the major splats pretty well, if we use it in the broad sense like nofather said.<br /> <br /> Vampires are possessed by their inner demon and animal instincts fused and dialed up to eleven.<br /> Werewolves are possessed by their spiritual heritage as descendants of the God of the Hunt.<br /> Mages are possessed by the Supernal.<br /> Changelings are possessed by the Land of Faerie and the Wyrd.<br /> The Bound are possessed by minor death-gods who are actually old ghosts.<br /> Among mummies, each of the Deceived are possessed by one-seventh of an eternally broken and tormented god.<br /> Beasts are possessed by the recurring nightmares of humanity.<br /> <br /> Demons don't count because they're the ones doing the possessing (well, more like stealing the right to exist itself, but still), and Prometheans ruin everything.<br /> <hr /><br /> Anyways, back to topic - I take back my earlier post, and newly suggest the somewhat niche case of &quot;A changeling whom you are a fetch of&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:25:18-08:00","id":1023260,"title":"","content":"Beasts of the Primordial variety. Literally defined by being scary. They're living nightmares. They specialize in scaring the bajeezes out of people by nature and inclination. They have numerous abilities that specifically operate around fear, and I'm not just talking about Nightmares. People here are talking about specific things they find creepy or scary. Beasts cover all of that, and more. There's a reason that Beast is the game that came up with the idea of an Apex.<br /> <br /> Every splat has its specialties. Being a horror is Beast's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:35:48-08:00","id":1023267,"title":"","content":"Shit, which one would NOT scare me senseless when I'd have to share a room with it?<br /> But IMO the less I could relate, the scarier it would be: Vampires are scary, but the wolfman would be scarier, and the Cthulhu-ripoff would be even worse.<br /> <br /> So, if PC-Splats, it'd be a Beast for me, if anything goes, and Idigam or Abyssal, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What would be the worst experience of all though?<br /> A Changeling telling me I'm his Fetch.<br /> That thought alone gives me goosebumps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:19:05-08:00","id":1023287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1023267#post1023267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shit, which one would NOT scare me senseless when I'd have to share a room with it?<br /> But IMO the less I could relate, the scarier it would be: Vampires are scary, but the wolfman would be scarier, and the Cthulhu-ripoff would be even worse.<br /> <br /> So, if PC-Splats, it'd be a Beast for me, if anything goes, and Idigam or Abyssal, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What would be the worst experience of all though?<br /> A Changeling telling me I'm his Fetch.<br /> That thought alone gives me goosebumps.</div> </div> </div> </div> I was leaning towards Beasts, both because the first story of the Beast anthology and because of the, strong arguments in this thread, but a Changeling that looks just like you telling you that your his fetch is brilliantly scary. <br /> <br /> Your right though, they can all be terrorifying. Imagine sharing a elevator with a man or woman you find cute, and all of a sudden for some reason that going into a rage and become this massive werewolf monster, and it's pisses and starts trashing the elevator. <br /> <br /> So many scenarios.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:35:17-08:00","id":1023293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1023267#post1023267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shit, which one would NOT scare me senseless when I'd have to share a room with it?<br /> But IMO the less I could relate, the scarier it would be: Vampires are scary, but the wolfman would be scarier, and the Cthulhu-ripoff would be even worse.<br /> <br /> So, if PC-Splats, it'd be a Beast for me, if anything goes, and Idigam or Abyssal, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> What would be the worst experience of all though?<br /> A Changeling telling me I'm his Fetch.<br /> That thought alone gives me goosebumps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about what mcn said and what you said made me realize something Beasts can make you feel like a fetch with a nightmare kinship already in the core called <br /> <br /> you Are an Impostor (Mannikin Changeling)<br /> The person becomes convinced that he is replica of the Beast and guess what depending on how much power the beast pumps in the guy hit with this can't feel anything no pain no joy no sorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 12-28-2016, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:22:42-08:00","id":1023311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1023293#post1023293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thinking about what mcn said and what you said made me realize something Beasts can make you feel like a fetch with a nightmare kinship already in the core called<br /> <br /> you Are an Impostor (Mannikin Changeling)<br /> The person becomes convinced that he is replica of the Beast and guess what depending on how much power the beast pumps in the guy hit with this can't feel anything no pain no joy no sorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I actually totally forgot about the Beast Nightmares.<br /> While I do not think that alone would make me more afraid of sharing space with a Beast (at least, not more than the thought of a Mage or Vampire fussing around with my mind), the effects of those nightmares.... oh-boy.<br /> All of a sudden becoming catatonically scared, unable to do something other than closing your eyes and hoping IT will pass? Suddenly remembering NOTHING about yourself? Out of the blue feeling watched, no matter what you do, and the feeling returns, and returns, and returns...? The sensation of scorpions/spiders/snakes/whatever crawling/slithering under your clothes? Being convinced that you're suddenly decaying rapidly?<br /> <br /> Horror. Pure, unadulterated horror.<br /> <br /> Mages are easily capable of doing this to you, too, though. (At least, those with Mind/Prime can.)<br /> <br /> Anything about Fetches is horryfing though, no matter whether it's you or loved ones that are affected.<br /> Remember how Dad changed, how he stopping drinking few years back? Well, surprise, it's not really your dad who stopped drinking! And the old one just came back to kill the thing that treated you better than he ever has!<br /> Remember how your son lost all interest in school, and you tried everything but the kid just seems bent on becoming criminal? No worries, it's an imposter! You never noticed, did you? Your real son has been abducted from right under your nose and was abused and survived hell and is now older than you, though. Never lost his interest in school, though, so there's that.<br /> Remember your wife? You fell in love with her in highschool, married early, you have a kid and a dog and a house and everything. Turns out, she's just bits of string and shadow without a soul, and the real her has been replaced back before you guys became a couple. The real deal hates your guts, wants to murder your wife and child and &quot;take back her life&quot;. Are you gonna let her?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T10:29:36-08:00","id":1023337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1023311#post1023311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I actually totally forgot about the Beast Nightmares.<br /> While I do not think that alone would make me more afraid of sharing space with a Beast (at least, not more than the thought of a Mage or Vampire fussing around with my mind), the effects of those nightmares.... oh-boy.<br /> All of a sudden becoming catatonically scared, unable to do something other than closing your eyes and hoping IT will pass? Suddenly remembering NOTHING about yourself? Out of the blue feeling watched, no matter what you do, and the feeling returns, and returns, and returns...? The sensation of scorpions/spiders/snakes/whatever crawling/slithering under your clothes? Being convinced that you're suddenly decaying rapidly?<br /> <br /> Horror. Pure, unadulterated horror.<br /> <br /> Mages are easily capable of doing this to you, too, though. (At least, those with Mind/Prime can.)<br /> <br /> Anything about Fetches is horryfing though, no matter whether it's you or loved ones that are affected.<br /> Remember how Dad changed, how he stopping drinking few years back? Well, surprise, it's not really your dad who stopped drinking! And the old one just came back to kill the thing that treated you better than he ever has!<br /> Remember how your son lost all interest in school, and you tried everything but the kid just seems bent on becoming criminal? No worries, it's an imposter! You never noticed, did you? Your real son has been abducted from right under your nose and was abused and survived hell and is now older than you, though. Never lost his interest in school, though, so there's that.<br /> Remember your wife? You fell in love with her in highschool, married early, you have a kid and a dog and a house and everything. Turns out, she's just bits of string and shadow without a soul, and the real her has been replaced back before you guys became a couple. The real deal hates your guts, wants to murder your wife and child and &quot;take back her life&quot;. Are you gonna let her?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Reading your description of fetched then unchained are the powered up version of them let's see can potentially become anyone can lie with no one the wiser can control their bodies giving them the ability to control their emotion from anyone even with super natural powers oh and also can remember anything and speak any language and that's not involving their demonic form ,embed and exploits also this kinda important they literally have to strip humans for their identity. <br /> <br /> Also for the whole mage can do it with prime/mind can do it I'd like to point out a couple of nightmares that beast have access to<br /> You Are Lost (Changeling)<br /> Victim gains the lost condition does not sound to bad <br /> Satiety expenditure: when the victim fails a navigation roll. The victim\u2019s hallucinations guide him into one of the many alternate realities that abut the physical world: the Shadow, the Underworld, or the Hedge, for example. The Beast has no control over exactly where the victim winds up. <br /> <br /> The Void Is Waiting (Low-Wisdom Mage)<br /> Magic is cast near person roll Resolve + Composure or Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance if not. Success for the victim means the power targets the victim rather than its intended target.<br /> <br /> Also behold my true form which generally if the person is killed is eighter turned to stone or any other material <br /> <br /> While Mages can do a lot of things Beasts can do but they can't do everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T12:42:01-08:00","id":1023383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1023337#post1023337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reading your description of fetched then unchained are the powered up version of them let's see can potentially become anyone can lie with no one the wiser can control their bodies giving them the ability to control their emotion from anyone even with super natural powers oh and also can remember anything and speak any language and that's not involving their demonic form ,embed and exploits also this kinda important they literally have to strip humans for their identity.<br /> <br /> Also for the whole mage can do it with prime/mind can do it I'd like to point out a couple of nightmares that beast have access to<br /> You Are Lost (Changeling)<br /> Victim gains the lost condition does not sound to bad<br /> Satiety expenditure: when the victim fails a navigation roll. The victim\u2019s hallucinations guide him into one of the many alternate realities that abut the physical world: the Shadow, the Underworld, or the Hedge, for example. The Beast has no control over exactly where the victim winds up.<br /> <br /> The Void Is Waiting (Low-Wisdom Mage)<br /> Magic is cast near person roll Resolve + Composure or Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance if not. Success for the victim means the power targets the victim rather than its intended target.<br /> <br /> Also behold my true form which generally if the person is killed is eighter turned to stone or any other material<br /> <br /> While Mages can do a lot of things Beasts can do but they can't do everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think the Fetch is more horrifying. A: the original is still around somewhere, being tortured and living through hell. Being non-existant is coming out ahead in comparison to me. And B: The Demon has a very palpable, understandable goal for what he does (supernatural fugitive from an oppressive regime, basically). The Fair Folk is basically just fooling around, and a fetch is nothing than an afterthought, made from junk. Call me crazy, but if I had to choose who'd take my identity, I'd take the one I can pity, despite all his might.<br /> <br /> Totally agree on that Beasts can pull stuff that Mages cannot, just wanted to point out that Nightmares are not what makes me more afraid of them than I am of Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T19:31:14-08:00","id":1023548,"title":"","content":"In that I will agree with Wormwood. The true horror of a Fetch isn't the ability of the creature to mirror someone. With enough time and practice, any splat, or even a clever mortal, can do the same.<br /> <br /> No, it is the implications of a Fetch. Be it negligence, be it a sudden moral conundrum, it resides in the fact that the Fetch isn't real, but at the same time that the Fetch can't be anything else.<br /> <br /> Absolutely no other splat can achieve this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T04:31:00-08:00","id":1023672,"title":"","content":"The horror of the Fetch isn't that it mimics you, it's in finding out that YOUR the Fetch, that your whole life is built on a lie, that you may not even have a soul, that your a made thing , not born.<br /> <br /> And if that isn't enough the person whose life you stole is back, they're pissed, and they have magical powers, a support organization, and more knowledge then you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T05:27:41-08:00","id":1023687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>backtoback</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1022673#post1022673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't go wrong with a Screaming Moon Cahalith</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTo be fair, a Banshee would mostly be interested in a thread like this precisely to find the most enjoyable prey possible, rather than wanting to measure how good it was at scaring mortals against such potential food.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T05:49:07-08:00","id":1023701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1023687#post1023687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bTo be fair, a Banshee would mostly be interested in a thread like this precisely to find the most enjoyable prey possible, rather than wanting to measure how good it was at scaring mortals against such potential food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking, I was referring to a Cahalith with the Screaming Moon Gift which doesn't require you to be in the Lodge of the same name(Damn Lunes!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T05:59:49-08:00","id":1023706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>backtoback</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1023701#post1023701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically speaking, I was referring to a Cahalith with the Screaming Moon Gift which doesn't require you to be in the Lodge of the same name(Damn Lunes!).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAh, that is true! Although a Cahalith with the Gift of the Screaming Moon who was a member of that Lodge would be somewhat of an apex of the whole matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:54:06-08:00","id":1023735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1023672#post1023672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The horror of the Fetch isn't that it mimics you, it's in finding out that YOUR the Fetch, that your whole life is built on a lie, that you may not even have a soul, that your a made thing , not born.<br /> <br /> And if that isn't enough the person whose life you stole is back, they're pissed, and they have magical powers, a support organization, and more knowledge then you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the fetch is poorly made, a murderous psycho about to explode, and his changeling counterpart\u00b4s return has managed to galvanize it. Oh, and he still live with the family. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T23:07:48-08:00","id":1024129,"title":"","content":"I wanted to throw this out there. Many games have groups that focus on fear, embodying it somehow or using it as a weapon. Often both. It's a pretty common thread.<br /> <br /> Vampire has the Nosferatu. Werewolf has the Lodge of the Screaming Moon, masters of fear and hunters of the feared, and the Lodge of the Hook Hand, who use fear as a tool to keep trespassers from their territories and explain their predation. Mage has the Fangs of Mara, who use the nightmares of the Abyss to strike at it. Changeling has the Autumn Court and to a more focused extent the Scarecrow Ministry, who are sort of like the Lodge of the Hook Hand, using and becoming urban legends to explain their feeding on the horror they inflict on mortals. And obviously there's Beast, who all feed on fear. <br /> <br /> There's probably more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T00:45:21-08:00","id":1024145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1024129#post1024129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to throw this out there. Many games have groups that focus on fear, embodying it somehow or using it as a weapon. Often both. It's a pretty common thread.<br /> <br /> Vampire has the Nosferatu. Werewolf has the Lodge of the Screaming Moon, masters of fear and hunters of the feared, and the Lodge of the Hook Hand, who use fear as a tool to keep trespassers from their territories and explain their predation. Mage has the Fangs of Mara, who use the nightmares of the Abyss to strike at it. Changeling has the Autumn Court and to a more focused extent the Scarecrow Ministry, who are sort of like the Lodge of the Hook Hand, using and becoming urban legends to explain their feeding on the horror they inflict on mortals. And obviously there's Beast, who all feed on fear.<br /> <br /> There's probably more.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Scarecrow Ministry remains one of my favorite CoD elements, ever. It was one of those things I saw and just went &quot;well THAT's what I want to play&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also let me throw in some love for the Hosts of Werewolf. The description of how one spider will paralyze you, and how you remain conscious while you see all its buddies arrive and eat you from the inside before taking your corpse for a joy ride, is one bit of text that remains with me to this day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:22:24-08:00","id":1026718,"title":"","content":"In monster splats Hosts. As well as the visceral &quot;ick&quot; of swarms of spiders and rats crawling into you, there's also the replacement factor. At least with a fetch, the original could be rescued and reclaim their life. With a host, they're gone, and only a hungry monster wearing their skin is left.<br /> <br /> In playable splats, probably demons. Similar irreversible replacement ideas, except this time there's literally no way to tell the difference until one day they explode into a bio-mechanical nightmare monster and wrathful angels start burning down your house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-09T08:15:15-08:00","id":1029078,"title":"","content":"To me, it's Changelings, Their powers is terrifying, they can make anyone go complete insane just tby showing up. People's minds are like putting on their hands, no one is safe if they want to they can make you a killer, make you gave everything you won to them, or just leave you as a terrifyed mess on the floor. And most important, they have reasons to do it. They alll have a target on their backs and almost all of them are prepared to anything to not go back, they're prepared to destroy anyone who gets on the way<br /> <br /> Prometheans are a close second,ironically most of the things that makes them scary are not really their fault. First there's the fact all of them were made by people who were mad, only a obsessed broken human being creates Prometheans. And obviously, all prometheans only exist becauase someone died to make them, they are wearing the body of murdered people. And aboce all there's torment. Torment can turn even th emost compassionate of them into a murderous monster nd tunring all the love and compassion they feel into rage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T11:29:25-08:00","id":1029675,"title":"","content":"I would have to say demons from demon the decent<br /> <br /> They are a almost pure unknown. Hiding behind the faces everyone around you even your loved ones could be one. They are the unknown army around you waiting to come for you. Demon are the broken ones what of the non broken angels who if you fall into their plans they will make sure you fall into what ever the plan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T15:23:57-08:00","id":1029792,"title":"","content":"I would say Beasts personally. Something about the idea of being locked in a room with the original thing that made my ancestors piss themselves doesn't sound very appealing to me. After all they were scared for a reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11554-fate-inker","name":"Fate Inker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T16:09:19-08:00","id":1029815,"title":"","content":"biggest issue here is that Beasts are born to terrify, but it's harder to tell if they are objectively the scariest in terms of capability to harm and ruin lifes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T17:44:38-08:00","id":1029839,"title":"","content":"I'd say an Ashwood Abbey Hunter.<br /> There's an instance in the Slasher book of a bunch of Abbey Hunters <i>gang-raping</i> a Slasher &quot;like animals&quot;. Let that sink in for a moment. They are raping a serial killer.<br /> These are people who enjoy violating and brutalizing serial killers and monsters for fun and pleasure. And the worst part for me? They're technically 100% human.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12712-tezof","name":"Tezof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-10T17:54:04-08:00","id":1029840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tezof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1022153-scariest-fucker?p=1029839#post1029839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an instance in the Slasher book of a bunch of Abbey Hunters <i>gang-raping</i> a Slasher &quot;like animals&quot;. Let that sink in for a moment. They are raping a serial killer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you tell me what page that's on? I see them celebrating their hunts, and rumors of 'long pig' but